associatedCastelnuovoSurface -- Castelnuovo surface associated to a rational complete intersection of three quadrics in P^7
***************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        E = associatedCastelnuovoSurface X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note complete intersection of three quadrics in PP^7:
        IntersectionOfThreeQuadricsInP7,, containing a surface $S\subset Y$
        that admits a *note congruence: CongruenceOfCurves, of $(2e-1)$-secant
        curves of degree $e$ inside the *note ambient fivefold:
        ambientFivefold, $Y$ of the fourfold $X$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Singular: Singular, => ..., default value null, whether to
        transfer computation to Singular
      * Strategy => ..., default value null
      * *note Verbose: Verbose, => ..., default value false, request verbose
        feedback
  * Outputs:
      * E, the (minimal) Castelnuovo surface associated to $X$
  * Consequences:
      * building E will return the following four objects:
          * the dominant *note rational map:
            (MultiprojectiveVarieties)MultirationalMap, $\mu:Y\dashrightarrow
            W$ defined by the linear system of hypersurfaces of degree $2e-1$
            having points of multiplicity $e$ along $S$;
          * the *note surface: (MultiprojectiveVarieties)
            EmbeddedProjectiveVariety, $U\subset W$ determining the inverse map
            of the restriction of $\mu$ to $X$;
          * the *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of the exceptional curves on
            the surface $U$;
          * a *note rational map: (MultiprojectiveVarieties)MultirationalMap,
            of degree 1 from the surface $U$ to the minimal Castelnuovo surface
            $\widetilde{U}$.

Description
===========

For more details, see the paper On complete intersections of three quadrics in
P^7 (see https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.01773 ).

