        which takes a general point $p\in\mathbb{P}^5$ (that is, outside a
        certain proper Zariski closed subset of $\mathbb{P}^5$) and returns the
        unique rational curve of degree $e$, $(3e-1)$-secant to $S$, and
        passing through $p$ (an error is thrown if such a curve does not exist
        or is not unique)

