gushelMukaiFourfold -- make a special Gushel-Mukai fourfold
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        gushelMukaiFourfold(S,X)
  * Inputs:
      * S, an *note embedded projective variety:
        (MultiprojectiveVarieties)EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, a smooth
        irreducible surface $S\subset\mathbb{P}^8$
      * X, an *note embedded projective variety:
        (MultiprojectiveVarieties)EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, a smooth prime
        Fano fourfold $X\subset \mathbb{P}^8$ of degree 10 and sectional genus
        6, which contains the surface $S$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * InputCheck => ..., default value 1
      * *note Verbose: Verbose, => ..., default value false, request verbose
        feedback
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Gushel-Mukai fourfold: GushelMukaiFourfold,, the special
        Gushel-Mukai fourfold corresponding to the pair $(S,X)$

Description
===========

In the following example, we define a Gushel-Mukai fourfold containing a
so-called $\tau$-quadric.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K = ZZ/33331; x := gens ring PP_K^8;                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = projectiveVariety ideal(x_6-x_7, x_5, x_3-x_4, x_1, x_0-x_4,        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : ProjectiveVariety, surface in PP^8                                      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_2*x_7-x_4*x_8);                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : X = projectiveVariety ideal(x_4*x_6-x_3*x_7+x_1*x_8,                    |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : ProjectiveVariety, 4-dimensional subvariety of PP^8                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_4*x_5-x_2*x_7+x_0*x_8, x_3*x_5-x_2*x_6+x_0*x_8+x_1*x_8-x_5*x_8,            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_1*x_5-x_0*x_6+x_0*x_7+x_1*x_7-x_5*x_7,                                     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_1*x_2-x_0*x_3+x_0*x_4+x_1*x_4-x_2*x_7+x_0*x_8,                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_0^2+x_0*x_1+x_1^2+x_0*x_2+2*x_0*x_3+x_1*x_3+x_2*x_3+x_3^2-x_0*x_4-x_1*x_4-2|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|*x_2*x_4-x_3*x_4-2*x_4^2+x_0*x_5+x_2*x_5+x_5^2+2*x_0*x_6+x_1*x_6+2*x_2*x_6+x_|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3*x_6+x_5*x_6+x_6^2-3*x_4*x_7+2*x_5*x_7-x_7^2+x_1*x_8+x_3*x_8-3*x_4*x_8+2*x_5|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|*x_8+x_6*x_8-x_7*x_8);                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : F = gushelMukaiFourfold(S,X);                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : ProjectiveVariety, GM fourfold containing a surface of degree 2 and     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|sectional genus 0                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : describe F                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = Special Gushel-Mukai fourfold of discriminant 10(')                     |
|     containing a surface of degree 2 and sectional genus 0                  |
|     cut out by 6 hypersurfaces of degrees 1^5 2^1                           |
|     and with class in G(1,4) given by s_(3,1)+s_(2,2)                       |
|     Type: ordinary                                                          |
|     (case 1 of Table 1 in arXiv:2002.07026)                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert(F == X)                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

