parameterCount -- count of parameters
*************************************

  * Usage: 
        parameterCount(S,X)
  * Inputs:
      * S, an *note embedded projective variety:
        (MultiprojectiveVarieties)EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,
      * X, an *note embedded projective variety:
        (MultiprojectiveVarieties)EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, such that
        $S\subseteq X$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Verbose: Verbose, => ..., default value false, request verbose
        feedback
  * Outputs:
      * a count of parameters to estimate the dimensions of the corresponding
        Hilbert schemes

Description
===========

See *note parameterCount(CubicFourfold): parameterCount_lpCubicFourfold_rp, and
*note parameterCount(GushelMukaiFourfold):
parameterCount_lpGushelMukaiFourfold_rp, for more precise applications of this
function.

The following calculation shows that the family of complete intersections of 3
quadrics in $\mathbb{P}^5$ containing a rational normal quintic curve has
codimension 1 in the space of all such complete intersections.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K = ZZ/33331; S = PP_K^(1,5);                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety, curve in PP^5                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : X = random({{2},{2},{2}},S);                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : ProjectiveVariety, surface in PP^5                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : time parameterCount(S,X,Verbose=>true)                                  |
| -- used 0.407542s (cpu); 0.279766s (thread); 0s (gc)                        |
|S: rational normal curve of degree 5 in PP^5                                 |
|X: smooth surface of degree 8 and sectional genus 5 in PP^5 cut              |
|(assumption: h^1(N_{S,P^5}) = 0)                                             |
|h^0(N_{S,P^5}) = 32                                                          |
|h^1(O_S(2)) = 0, and h^0(I_{S,P^5}(2)) = 10 = h^0(O_(P^5)(2)) -              |
|in particular, h^0(I_{S,P^5}(2)) is minimal                                  |
|dim GG(2,9) = 21                                                             |
|h^0(N_{S,P^5}) + dim GG(2,9) = 53                                            |
|h^0(N_{S,X}) = 0                                                             |
|dim{[X] : S ⊂ X} >= 53                                                       |
|dim GG(2,P(H^0(O_(P^5)(2)))) = 54                                            |
|codim{[X] : S ⊂ X} <= 1                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = (1, (10, 32, 0))                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Sequence                                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|out by 3 hypersurfaces of degree 2                                           |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|\chi(O_S(2));                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

