specialFourfold -- make a Hodge-special fourfold
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        specialFourfold(S,X,V)
        specialFourfold(S,X)
        specialFourfold S
  * Inputs:
      * S, an *note embedded projective variety:
        (MultiprojectiveVarieties)EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, an irreducible
        *note surface: surface,
      * X, an *note embedded projective variety:
        (MultiprojectiveVarieties)EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, a smooth fourfold
        $X$ containing the surface $S$
      * V, an *note embedded projective variety:
        (MultiprojectiveVarieties)EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, optional, a *note
        fivefold: ambientFivefold, where X is a hypersurface
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * InputCheck => ..., default value 1
      * NumNodes => ..., default value null
      * *note Verbose: Verbose, => ..., default value false, request verbose
        feedback
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Hodge-special fourfold: HodgeSpecialFourfold,, which
        corresponds to the pair $(S,X)$

Description
===========

This can also be used as a shortcut for both *note cubicFourfold:
cubicFourfold, and *note gushelMukaiFourfold: gushelMukaiFourfold,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = surface {3,4};                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : ProjectiveVariety, surface in PP^5                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = specialFourfold S -- a random cubic fourfold through S              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = X                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : ProjectiveVariety, cubic fourfold containing a surface of degree 5 and  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|sectional genus 1                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : describe X                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Special cubic fourfold of discriminant 14                               |
|     containing a rational surface of degree 5 and sectional genus 1         |
|     cut out by 5 hypersurfaces of degree 2                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Y = specialFourfold "tau-quadric" -- a random GM fourfold through a     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = Y                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : ProjectiveVariety, GM fourfold containing a surface of degree 2 and     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|tau-quadric                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|sectional genus 0                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : describe Y                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = Special Gushel-Mukai fourfold of discriminant 10(')                     |
|     containing a surface of degree 2 and sectional genus 0                  |
|     cut out by 6 hypersurfaces of degrees 1^5 2^1                           |
|     and with class in G(1,4) given by s_(3,1)+s_(2,2)                       |
|     Type: ordinary                                                          |
|     (case 1 of Table 1 in arXiv:2002.07026)                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : T = surface {3,2};                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : ProjectiveVariety, surface in PP^7                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : Z = specialFourfold T -- a random c. i. of 3 quadrics through T         |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = Z                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : ProjectiveVariety, complete intersection of three quadrics in PP^7      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|containing a surface of degree 7 and sectional genus 1                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : describe Z                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = Complete intersection of 3 quadrics in PP^7                             |
|     of discriminant 79 = det| 8 7  |                                        |
|                             | 7 16 |                                        |
|     containing a rational surface of degree 7 and sectional genus 1         |
|     cut out by 14 hypersurfaces of degree 2                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

