surface(List) -- get a rational surface
***************************************

  * Function: *note surface: surface,
  * Usage: 
        surface {a,i,j,k,...}
        surface({a,i,j,k,...),K)
        surface({a,i,j,k,...},K,NumNodes=>n,ambient=>m)
  * Inputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list $\{a,i,j,k,\ldots\}$ of
        nonnegative integers
  * Outputs:
      * an *note embedded projective variety:
        (MultiprojectiveVarieties)EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,, the image of the
        rational map defined by the linear system of curves of degree $a$ in
        $\mathbb{P}_{K}^2$ having $i$ random base points of multiplicity 1, $j$
        random base points of multiplicity 2, $k$ random base points of
        multiplicity 3, and so on until the last integer in the given list.

Description
===========

In the example below, we take the image of the rational map defined by the
linear system of septic plane curves with 3 random simple base points and 9
random double points.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = surface {7,3,9};                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : ProjectiveVariety, surface in PP^5                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : coefficientRing S                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|       ZZ                                                                    |
|o2 = -----                                                                   |
|     65521                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : T = surface({7,3,9},ZZ/33331);                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : ProjectiveVariety, surface in PP^5                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : X = cubicFourfold T;                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : ProjectiveVariety, cubic fourfold containing a surface of degree 10 and |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|sectional genus 6                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : coefficientRing X                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|       ZZ                                                                    |
|o5 = -----                                                                   |
|     33331                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : describe X                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = Special cubic fourfold of discriminant 26                               |
|     containing a rational surface of degree 10 and sectional genus 6        |
|     cut out by 10 hypersurfaces of degree 3                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note rationalMap(PolynomialRing,List):
    (Cremona)rationalMap_lpPolynomialRing_cmList_rp, -- rational map defined by
    the linear system of hypersurfaces passing through random points with
    multiplicity
  * *note gushelMukaiFourfold(Array,Array):
    gushelMukaiFourfold_lpArray_cmArray_cmString_cmThing_rp, -- construct GM
    fourfolds by gluing cubic or quartic scrolls to surfaces in PP^6

