trisecantFlop -- examples of trisecant flops
********************************************

  * Usage: 
        trisecantFlop i
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an integer between 0 and 17
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Verbose: Verbose, => ..., default value false, request verbose
        feedback
  * Outputs:
      * the i-th example of birational map $X\dashrightarrow W$ in accordance
        to the Table 1 in the paper Trisecant Flops, their associated K3
        surfaces and the rationality of some Fano fourfolds (see
        https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.01263 ).

Description
===========

This function requires the package TrisecantFlops (see
https://github.com/giovannistagliano/TrisecantFlops ). If not present the user
will be asked to automatically install the package.

See also
========

  * *note specialFourfold(String,ZZ): specialFourfold_lpString_cmZZ_rp, -- load
    a prebuilt example of fourfold

